  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing community stabilization in central Chad: Kanem, Barh el Gazel and Batha</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Communities in Kanem, Barh El Ghazel, and Batha in Chad face interconnected challenges that intensify socio-economic instability. Factors such as limited government presence, poor infrastructure, and the impacts of climate change have disrupted agropastoral livelihoods and agricultural productivity, forcing households to adopt negative coping mechanisms such as distress sales of livestock. This project focuses on two main pillars (diversification of livelihood and access to basic services) and implements targeted activities in 15 selected communities in the provinces of Kanem, Bar el Gazel and Batha. The main objective of the project is to enhance stability of communities and foster sustainable development in the target localities by addressing critical challenges related to basic infrastructure and livelihoods through inclusive governance and locally led conflict mediation efforts that strengthen social cohesion and community resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
